<section class="band band--sand">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>Four methods, interlocking</h2>
    <p>Not four alternatives to choose between. They run together, and which one leads at a
    given moment is a clinical decision rather than something you pick in advance.</p>
    <div class="pathways">
      <a href="/approach/narm/">
        <h3>NARM</h3>
        <p>The pattern underneath, where it was learned, and what choice you have once you can
        see it happening rather than only feel it.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/approach/somatic-experiencing/">
        <h3>Somatic Experiencing</h3>
        <p>Shock trauma met a little at a time, slow and gentle, building your window of
        tolerance rather than testing it.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/approach/emdr/">
        <h3>EMDR</h3>
        <p>What EMDR actually involves, who it suits, and what tends to be behind it when it
        has stalled somewhere before.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/approach/ifs-informed-emdr/">
        <h3>IFS-informed EMDR</h3>
        <p>Reem's main focus. The protective parts of you are consulted before anything is
        processed, and most of the emphasis sits in that preparation.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p><a href="/approach/">How the four fit together, in plain language</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shell band faq">
  <h2>Common questions about therapy here</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>How much does a therapy session cost?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>$240 for a 50-minute online session with Reem, self-pay. Trail walk and movement
      sessions are $125 for an hour. The practice's LPC Associates see clients
      at lower fees, including sliding scale.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Do you take insurance?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Blue Cross Blue Shield is accepted. Sessions under any other plan are self-pay, by
      major credit card. If you plan to seek out-of-network reimbursement from another insurer,
      raise it in the consult so you know what documentation to expect.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Is therapy in person or online?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Online across Texas is the default. In person means trail walk and movement therapy on
      Fridays, or equine sessions near Dripping Springs, both for adults, both after a consult
      and one to three online sessions.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>What happens in a first session?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Mostly orientation: what brought you, what you want different, what your nervous system
      does under stress, and how we will pace the work. Nothing about trauma gets opened faster
      than you can stay present for.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Which page should I read?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Start with whichever of trauma, anxiety, depression or walk and talk sounds most like
      your week. They overlap a great deal, and you do not have to sort yourself correctly
      before a consult. The approach page explains the methods that run through all of them.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>What if I need help sooner than you have openings?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Ask about the associates, who generally have availability sooner and lower fees. If
      neither fits, Reem will refer you out rather than leave you on a waitlist. If you are in
      immediate danger, call 911; for a mental health crisis, call or text 988.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>

